Flag file entries such as: --js='/usr/my project/app.js' are split on whitespace such that &quot;/usr/my&quot; and &quot;project/app.js&quot; are treated as separate tokens.

The attached patch corrects this issue using a custom tokenizer method tokenizeKeepingQuotedStrings(). The following JUnit test was used in a separate project to test this method:

@Test public void tokenizeKeepingQuotedStrings() {
  String data = &quot;t1 \&quot;t2\&quot; t3='quoted string' --t4=\&quot;/my project/app.js\&quot; &quot;
      + String.format(&quot;%n&quot;) + &quot;'adjacent content't5 t6='single'&quot;;
  List&lt;String&gt; tokens = StringUtil.tokenizeKeepingQuotedStrings(data);
  List&lt;String&gt; expected = ImmutableList.of(&quot;t1&quot;, &quot;\&quot;t2\&quot;&quot;, &quot;t3='quoted string'&quot;,
      &quot;--t4=\&quot;/my project/app.js\&quot;&quot;, &quot;'adjacent content't5&quot;, &quot;t6='single'&quot;);
  assertEquals(expected, tokens);
}

The patch has been tested on a small project using a flag file. In addition, &quot;ant test&quot; ran successfully.

